🗣️ EnglishSaathi — Your Personal AI English-Speaking Coach

A Streamlit chatbot that:

Understands Hindi, Marathi, English, or a mix of all three
Translates your Hindi/Marathi into English
Corrects your English mistakes and explains them in simple Hindi/Marathi
Replies like a friendly conversation partner (in English) to keep you practicing
Lets you speak to it (mic) and hear it (voice reply)
Runs free, and works on your phone once deployed

It uses Groq (free tier) as the AI engine — one model for chat/translation/correction (llama-3.3-70b-versatile) and one for voice-to-text (whisper-large-v3). Voice output uses your phone/browser's own built-in voice (no extra cost).

0. What you need before starting
A computer to do the one-time setup (phone alone won't work for this step)
A free GitHub account → https://github.com/join
A free Streamlit Community Cloud account → https://share.streamlit.io (sign in with GitHub)
A free Groq API key → https://console.groq.com (sign up → left sidebar API Keys → Create API Key)
Python 3.9+ installed if you want to test locally first (optional but recommended)
1. Get your Groq API key
Go to https://console.groq.com and sign up (free, no card needed).
Left sidebar → API Keys → Create API Key.
Copy the key (starts with gsk_...). Keep it safe — you'll paste it in two places below.
2. Test the app on your computer first (recommended)
Download/unzip these files into one folder, e.g. englishsaathi/:
app.py
requirements.txt
.streamlit/secrets.toml.example
Rename .streamlit/secrets.toml.example → .streamlit/secrets.toml (keep the .streamlit folder name exactly as-is).
Open that secrets.toml file and paste your real key:
   GROQ_API_KEY = "gsk_your_real_key_here"
Open a terminal in the englishsaathi/ folder and run:
bash
   python -m venv venv
   # Windows:
   venv\Scripts\activate
   # Mac/Linux:
   source venv/bin/activate

   pip install -r requirements.txt
   streamlit run app.py
Your browser opens http://localhost:8501. Allow microphone permission when asked.
Try typing "मुझे नौकरी के इंटरव्यू में घबराहट होती है" or tap 🎤 and speak — check you get a translation + a friendly English reply, and that "🔊 Listen" plays audio.

If you hit an error here, copy the exact error text and share it — that's the fastest way to fix it.

3. Put the code on GitHub
Go to https://github.com/new → name the repo englishsaathi → Create repository.
Upload the same files (app.py, requirements.txt, and the .streamlit folder) using "Add file → Upload files" on the GitHub repo page.
⚠️ Do NOT upload your real secrets.toml (the one with your actual key) to GitHub — only the .example one, or nothing at all. You'll add the real key in Streamlit Cloud's secrets in the next step (that one stays private).
4. Deploy for free on Streamlit Community Cloud
Go to https://share.streamlit.io → Create app → From an existing repo.
Pick your englishsaathi repo, branch main, main file path app.py.
Click Advanced settings → Secrets → paste:
   GROQ_API_KEY = "gsk_your_real_key_here"
Click Deploy. Wait 1-2 minutes for the build to finish.
You'll get a public link like https://englishsaathi-yourname.streamlit.app.
5. Use it on your phone like an app
Open that link in your phone's browser (Chrome recommended for full mic support).
Allow microphone access when prompted.
Tap your browser's menu → "Add to Home Screen". It now opens full-screen from your home screen, just like a regular app icon.
6. How to actually use it
Sidebar: set your level (Beginner/Intermediate/Advanced) and which language (Hindi/Marathi/Hinglish) you want mistakes explained in.
Type or tap 🎤 and talk naturally — Hindi, Marathi, English, or mixed.
Each reply shows, when relevant:
🌐 the English translation of what you said
✏️ your English attempt → ✅ the corrected version → why it was wrong
💬 a short friendly English reply + follow-up question, so you keep talking
🔊 Listen button to hear it pronounced correctly (auto-plays if enabled in the sidebar)
Clear conversation in the sidebar to start a fresh session.
7. Notes, limits & troubleshooting
Cost: Groq's free tier is generous for personal daily practice, but has per-minute request limits. If you see a 429 error, wait a minute and try again.
Mic not working / no sound:
Make sure you tapped Allow for microphone permission.
Voice output (speechSynthesis) works best on Chrome/Edge (Android & desktop). On iPhone Safari, voice output support is inconsistent — text will still show correctly either way.
Voice input (recording → Whisper) works on all modern browsers since it just uploads audio.
"GROQ_API_KEY not found" error: you likely forgot step 2.3 (local) or step 4.3 (cloud).
App feels slow the first time you open it after inactivity: free Streamlit Cloud apps "sleep" after inactivity and take ~30-60 seconds to wake up. This is normal on the free tier.
Want changes (different look, add pronunciation scoring, save chat history, etc.)? Just ask — share the error text if something breaks and it'll be quick to fix.